\begin{lemma}[Consistency of the constructed paired-line measurement]
	\label{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.combined_line_measurement_consistency}
	\leanok
	\uses{lem:qld-4-10, lem:qld-comm-line-cons, lem:pasting-heterogeneous,
		def:concrete-paired-line-measurement, def:consistency}
	This is a formalization auxiliary lemma. Fix a polynomially small
	function $\delta_Q(\eps)$. There is a function
	$\delta_P(\eps,md/q)=\poly(\eps,md/q)$, in the corrected sum sense,
	such that for every projective strategy passing with error $\eps$ and
	every joint point family satisfying the conclusions of
	Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10} with error $\delta_Q(\eps)$, the concrete POVM
	\[
		T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}
		=\hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
		 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},Z),\ell_Z}_{f_Z}
		 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
	\]
	has evaluated consistency defect at most $\delta_P(\eps,md/q)$ with that
	joint point family, averaged over two independent line-point samples,
	for every directed opposite placement. The line-error function is chosen
	after $\delta_Q$ and its polynomial bound. This isolates the consistency
	part of the preceding construction while retaining its defining
	measurement; see \cite{gap:qpbt_subline-claims-line-marginal}.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	\leanok
	\uses{lem:qld-comm-line-cons, lem:pasting-heterogeneous,
		fact:agreement, fact:add-a-proj, lem:cool-closeness-fact,
		lem:schwartz-zippel-total-degree, def:line-point-dist,
		def:concrete-paired-line-measurement,
		lem:line-point-same-placement-distance,
		lem:coefficient-polynomial-agreement,
		lem:combined-line-conditioned-defect,
		lem:combined-line-restored-defect,
		thm:qld-conditioned-polynomial-bound}
	The two ordered-product comparisons imply the X and Z point-marginal
	bounds. Combining these with line-point consistency and line
	self-consistency, Lemma~\ref{lem:line-point-same-placement-distance},
	bounds each completed point-to-line marginal defect by
	$\Delta=8\delta_Q(\eps)+C(\eps+\sqrt{\eps})$, for a universal $C\ge1$.

	Condition the product line-point law on the X line having nonzero
	direction. Its retained mass $r$ is at least $1/2$, since every axis
	direction is nonzero. Resampling an independent uniform affine
	parameter preserves the line-point law. On each nondegenerate X line,
	the root bound of Lemma~\ref{lem:coefficient-polynomial-agreement}
	therefore gives conditional collision probability at most $md/q$.
	Both marginal defects under the restricted law are at most $\Delta/r$.

	Reindex the expanded state according to the chosen opposite placements,
	keeping the unused registers on the line-measurement side. Apply
	Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-heterogeneous} with answer order Z then X:
	its sandwich is precisely the X-Z-X POVM in the statement.
	Reversing both answer coordinates preserves the consistency defect.
	This is Lemma~\ref{lem:combined-line-conditioned-defect}.

	The discarded zero-direction mass is at most $1/(2q)$: it is zero
	for axis lines, and at most $1/q$ for diagonal lines, since their
	last direction coordinate is uniform. Every pointwise consistency
	defect lies in $[0,1]$. Restoring the original law gives the bound
	\[
		r\,\delta_{\mathrm{pasting}}(md/q,\Delta/r)+\frac1{2q},
	\]
	which is Lemma~\ref{lem:combined-line-restored-defect}. Take the
	minimum with the independent unit bound. Since $1/2\le r\le1$,
	$md\ge1$, and $\delta_Q$ is polynomially small,
	Theorem~\ref{thm:qld-conditioned-polynomial-bound} turns this into a
	uniform bound of the required corrected sum form.
	The same argument applies to every directed opposite placement.
\end{proof}

